    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12089" root="دبو and دبى" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ مَدْبِيَّةٌ</span></b>  (S, M, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَدْبُوَّةٌ</span></b> , (M, K,)
the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span> being substituted for the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span> as interchangeable therewith, (M,) <i>A land of which the herbage
has been eaten by</i> [<i>the locusts termed</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبًى</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبًا</span>.
(S, M, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Accord. to Z, both signify [also]
<i>A land that produces</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُبَّآء</span>, i. e. <i>gourds.</i> (TA in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دب</span>.)

